    Under the assumptions on $\Phi_m$ and $K$, there exists a one-parameter family of solutions $(W_K,c_K)$ of

\begin{align}
\label{eq:wave_eq}
c^2 \, W(x) &= - \suminf \Big( \int_{-\infty}^x \Phi_m'\big(\nu m - A_m W(\xi + \frac{m}{2} ) \big) - \Phi_m'\big(\nu m - A_m W(\xi - \frac{m}{2} ) \big) \, {\rm d} \xi \Big) + \eta \nonumber \\
&= - \suminf \Big( \int_{x-m}^x \Phi_m'\big(\nu m - A_m W(\xi + \frac{m}{2} ) \big) \, {\rm d} \xi \Big) + \eta \nonumber \\
&= - \suminf \Big( \int_{-\frac{m}{2}}^{\frac{m}{2}} \Phi_m'\big(\nu m - A_m W(x + \xi ) \big) \, {\rm d} \xi \Big) + \eta\nonumber \\
&= \suminf \big( A_m (- \Phi_m'(\nu m - A_m W(x) ) ) \big)  + \eta,
\end{align}

with $\|W_K\|^2_2= 2K$.

