mcq.question:
Let $N\ge 1$, let $0<\gamma<\min\{2,N\}$, let $u_0\ge 0$ on $\mathbb{R}^N$, and let $f\in S_q$ with $q\in[1,\infty)$. Assume that at least one of the following sets of conditions holds:

(i) $r>\dfrac{N}{2-\gamma}$, $q<1+r$, and $F(u_0)^{-r}\in L^{1}_{\mathrm{ul}}(\mathbb{R}^N)$;

(ii) $r>\dfrac{N}{2-\gamma}$, $q=1+r$, $F(u_0)^{-r}\in L^{1}_{\mathrm{ul}}(\mathbb{R}^N)$, and $f'(\xi)F(\xi)\le q$ for all sufficiently large $\xi>0$;

(iii) $r=\dfrac{N}{2-\gamma}$, $q<1+r$, and $F(u_0)^{-r}\in \mathcal{L}^{1}_{\mathrm{ul}}(\mathbb{R}^N)$.

Under these assumptions, which statement asserts the existence of an object satisfying the stated properties?

