\section{ Construction of subsolutions}\label{subsolution}

The goal of this section is to prove Theorem~\ref{thm1_1}. Our approach is similar to that in Tao--Winkler, “2025-JDE-TaoWinkler”; however, the parameters $\alpha$ and $\beta$ used in our construction are chosen differently. 

\begin{lem}\label{alphabeta-lem}
Let $n \geq 3$. Assume that $ p,q <1$ and satisfy $(\ref{pq})$. Then one can find constants $\alpha, \beta \in (0, 1-\frac{1}{n})$ and $\delta \in (0,\frac{1}{n})$ such that
\begin{align}\label{pq-2}
(1-\beta)(1-p)-\delta>0, \quad (1-\alpha)(1-q)-\delta>0
\end{align}
In this step, the authors construct subsolutions, which have the same form as those in Tao--Winkler, “2025-JDE-TaoWinkler”, to detect finite-time blow-up.

